===BODY===
          <h2>Across the Irish Sea</h2>
          <p>Cars come back from Ireland on the Irish Sea ferries, such as Dublin to Holyhead or Liverpool, and Rosslare to Fishguard or Pembroke. Which crossing makes sense depends on where the car is in Ireland and where it's going in Great Britain, and we include it in one fixed price.</p>

          <h2>Where we collect from</h2>
          <p>We collect from anywhere in the Republic of Ireland: Dublin, Cork, Galway, Limerick, Waterford, Kerry, Donegal and the ferry ports. If your car broke down on the way to a ferry, we can collect it from near the terminal.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Tip:</strong> leave the keys and a note with the garage or the person looking after the car, take photos, and send us the exact address and a contact name. Then you can travel home as a foot passenger or by plane.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>Insurance</h2>
          <p>Check whether your breakdown or car insurance covers repatriation from Ireland. If you need to arrange it yourself, we'll give you a written quote you can send to your insurer.</p>
===FAQ===
Q: Do you collect from Northern Ireland as well?
A: Northern Ireland is part of the UK, so that's a standard vehicle transport job. Ask us for a quote and we'll bring the car to Great Britain.
Q: How long does it take?
A: Timing depends on the location and the ferry schedules. We'll give you an expected collection and delivery time with the quote.
Q: Can you bring back a non-runner?
A: Yes. Tell us that it doesn't run or roll when you ask for a quote.
